WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:00.893
Quick recap.

00:00:01.114 --> 00:00:04.399
Step one: RNA polymerase makes contact at

00:00:04.446 --> 00:00:05.084
the promoter.

00:00:05.711 --> 00:00:08.103
Step two: proteins open up the DNA

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:08.498
there.

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:12.073
Step three: polymerase reads the template strand

00:00:12.224 --> 00:00:13.908
and builds matching RNA.

00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:16.276
The coding strand is not read.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.296
Like a train leaving the station on

00:00:18.377 --> 00:00:18.981
one track.

00:00:19.608 --> 00:00:21.384
RNA polymerase starts at the promoter and

00:00:21.431 --> 00:00:22.638
reads the template strand.

00:00:23.265 --> 00:00:24.484
Let's see what you remember.
